 # envbox
 
+Experimental integration probe: a `:managed` CODER_MOUNTS option skips
+Envbox's chmod/chown on that mount. The volume provider must present ownership
+appropriate for the inner user namespace. This does not disable Sysbox checks.
+
 ## Introduction
 
 `envbox` is an image that enables creating non-privileged containers capable of running system-level software (e.g. `dockerd`, `systemd`, etc) in Kubernetes.
